<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    Templated from VFEP's VFEP_Warcasket_Siegebreaker (VFEP commit e237aba,
    1.6/Defs/ThingDefs_Misc/Apparel_Various.xml); fields not discussed here are Siegebreaker's,
    VFEP_SpacerWarcaskets research prereq included.

    Tuning. Reference numbers are VFEP's 10th-generation sets (Siegebreaker, Guardian,
    Controller, Sarcophagus, Brute). A close-combat suit pitched at Brute and Guardian
    effectiveness, priced a little under them:
    - ArmorRating_Blunt 1.5 (Brute and Guardian; the other three 1.0) on all three pieces, the
      Guardian pattern. Sharp 2 and Heat 1 are the shared spacer values.
    - EnergyShieldEnergyMax 2.0: above the 1.5 Guardian, Controller and Sarcophagus carry,
      under the Siegebreaker's 2.5, the "improved shield capacitors" that set is sold on (Brute
      5.0, melee-locked). The bubble blocks ranged fire only, what a melee suit needs while
      closing; the plating and the jump are where this set spends its budget.
    - costList ComponentSpacer 6 / Plasteel 180 / Uranium 50 (Siegebreaker 6 / 145 / 50,
      Guardian 6 / 200 / 50). VFEP uses the component count as a tech-complexity dial
      (Controller 12, the utility sets 6, Brute 4); a drop thruster is Aerial-tier tech, so 6,
      with the plating step priced onto plasteel. At market value (plasteel 9, component 200,
      uranium 6) the full set is about 4780 silver without Odyssey: Siegebreaker 4195,
      Sarcophagus 4785, Guardian 5164, Brute 5220. The shoulders and helmet scale at the
      10th-gen piece ratios; see their headers.
    - costList GravlitePanel 30 under Odyssey (10 each on the shoulders and helmet; cf. VGE2's
      combat vacsuit 20/10 split): the thrusters and the space flight are gravtech and live on
      this piece. A panel is market value 4 but needs vacstone, which only comes from space,
      so the 50-panel set total is a been-to-orbit gate rather than a silver one, and the space
      functionality is priced here rather than in the base costList.

    Abilities: VEF CompAbilitiesApparel grants SCWC_BreachJump (AbilityDefs/BreachJump.xml),
    fueled by the CompApparelReloadable beside it (Aerial's 100-charge chemfuel tank). The
    ability reads the tank off the apparel that grants it, so both comps must sit on this one
    def, which is why the engine is here and not on the shoulders as on Aerial.
    chargeNoun "fuel unit", not Aerial's "jump": the stats pane and reload text count the
    tank's charges under that noun, and a jump burns fuelPerJump of them, so "jump" reads as
    100 jumps per tank instead of 5. "Fuel" alone pluralizes badly, and it is not "chemfuel"
    because the VGE root switches the tank to astrofuel.
    SCWC_BreachJumpRange +20 is the set's whole planet-side range (StatDefs/BreachJumpRange.xml).

    apparel tags: WarcasketVeteran (VFEP's 10th-gen tag) puts the set on the veteran raid
    pawnkinds of both VFEP factions and Odyssey's VFEP_Salvager_Warcasket; WarcasketAll is
    VFEP_General. Threat and flavor only: AI pawns never cast apparel abilities and warcasket
    parts are destroyed on drop and untradeable, so the foundry is the only source.

    Compat patches reach this def from 1.6/Patches/SOS2Patch.xml (EVA tag, cold insulation) and
    the 1.6/Mods/VanillaGravshipExpanded/Patches/ root (vacuum resistance, space walking,
    astrofuel); see their headers.

    renderNodeProperties: the thruster-glow node (Source/1.6/Rendering/, alpha from the
    ability's thrusterGlowCurve). The art is desaturated and color tints it chemfuel orange,
    between the core and fringe of the VFEP_JumpFlame flecks; the VGE root recolors it purple.
    TransparentPostLight so it reads at night. parentTagDef ApparelBody puts it beside the
    armor's own node; baseLayer is only the fallback when that node is absent.

    ApparelExtension priority 1: VFEP_WarcasketArmorBase carries its own ApparelExtension and
    inheritance appends list items, so this def resolves with two. VEF merges duplicate
    extensions in a Def.ResolveReferences prefix, highest priority surviving, and
    ApparelExtension.Merge does not copy moveSpeedFactorByTerrainTag; at equal priority the
    parent's copy would win and drop VGE's space-walking factor. At priority 1 every field of
    ours, from any load root, is kept. The helmet and shoulders carry the same guard.
  -->
  <VFEPirates.WarcasketDef ParentName="VFEP_WarcasketArmorBase">
    <defName>SCWC_Warcasket_Shipcracker</defName>
    <label>shipcracker warcasket</label>
    <shortDescription>Specialized spacer-tech warcasket shell with improved impact dispersion, fitted with fuel-burning drop thrusters for breaching jumps and a ranged shield.</shortDescription>
    <description>Specialized spacer-tech warcasket shell with improved impact dispersion, fitted with fuel-burning drop thrusters for breaching jumps and a ranged shield.\n\nAn Imperial pattern, not a pirate one: boarding corps built it on the 10th-generation spacer chassis to cross the gap between two ships and open the far hull from the outside. Salvage and desertion have since put it in foundries far from any Imperial dock.\n\nA shipcracker launches through the vacuum, lands on the enemy hull, punches through to the interior and takes the ship room by room. Under gravity the same burn clears a wall or a roof in a single hop. The shield stops bullets, not blades: pilots are chosen for a taste for close work.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketShipcracker/WarcasketShipcracker</texPath>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <Mass>50</Mass>
      <ArmorRating_Sharp>2</ArmorRating_Sharp>
      <ArmorRating_Blunt>1.5</ArmorRating_Blunt>
      <ArmorRating_Heat>1</ArmorRating_Heat>
      <Insulation_Cold>80</Insulation_Cold>
      <Insulation_Heat>80</Insulation_Heat>
      <EquipDelay>1</EquipDelay>
      <EnergyShieldRechargeRate>0.01</EnergyShieldRechargeRate>
      <EnergyShieldEnergyMax>2.0</EnergyShieldEnergyMax>
    </statBases>
    <equippedStatOffsets>
      <PsychicSensitivity>-0.5</PsychicSensitivity>
      <ToxicResistance>0.5</ToxicResistance>
      <SlaveSuppressionOffset MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">0.3</SlaveSuppressionOffset>
      <VacuumResistance MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">0.2</VacuumResistance>
      <SCWC_BreachJumpRange>20</SCWC_BreachJumpRange>
    </equippedStatOffsets>
    <costList>
      <ComponentSpacer>6</ComponentSpacer>
      <Plasteel>180</Plasteel>
      <Uranium>50</Uranium>
      <GravlitePanel MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">30</GravlitePanel>
    </costList>
    <researchPrerequisites>
      <li>VFEP_SpacerWarcaskets</li>
    </researchPrerequisites>
    <apparel>
      <bodyPartGroups>
        <li>Torso</li>
        <li>Legs</li>
        <li>Feet</li>
      </bodyPartGroups>
      <wornGraphicPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketShipcracker/WarcasketShipcracker</wornGraphicPath>
      <renderNodeProperties>
        <li>
          <debugLabel>SCWC_ThrusterGlow</debugLabel>
          <nodeClass>ShipcrackerWarcasket.PawnRenderNode_ThrusterGlow</nodeClass>
          <workerClass>ShipcrackerWarcasket.PawnRenderNodeWorker_ThrusterGlow</workerClass>
          <parentTagDef>ApparelBody</parentTagDef>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketShipcracker/WarcasketShipcrackerThrusterGlow</texPath>
          <shaderTypeDef>TransparentPostLight</shaderTypeDef>
          <color>(1, 0.72, 0.38)</color>
          <baseLayer>31</baseLayer>
        </li>
      </renderNodeProperties>
      <layers>
        <li>OnSkin</li>
        <li>Middle</li>
        <li>Shell</li>
      </layers>
      <tags>
        <li>WarcasketVeteran</li>
        <li>WarcasketAll</li>
      </tags>
    </apparel>
    <comps>
      <li Class="CompProperties_ApparelReloadable">
        <maxCharges>100</maxCharges>
        <ammoDef>Chemfuel</ammoDef>
        <ammoCountPerCharge>1</ammoCountPerCharge>
        <baseReloadTicks>60</baseReloadTicks>
        <soundReload>Standard_Reload</soundReload>
        <hotKey>Misc4</hotKey>
        <chargeNoun>fuel unit</chargeNoun>
        <displayGizmoWhileUndrafted>false</displayGizmoWhileUndrafted>
      </li>
      <li Class="VEF.Abilities.CompProperties_AbilitiesApparel">
        <abilities>
          <li>SCWC_BreachJump</li>
        </abilities>
      </li>
      <li Class="VEF.Apparels.CompProperties_ShieldBubble">
        <compClass>VEF.Apparels.CompShieldBubble</compClass>
        <blockRangedAttack>true</blockRangedAttack>
        <blockMeleeAttack>false</blockMeleeAttack>
        <showWhenDrafted>true</showWhenDrafted>
        <showOnHostiles>true</showOnHostiles>
        <showOnNeutralInCombat>true</showOnNeutralInCombat>
        <shieldTexPath>Other/ShieldBubble</shieldTexPath>
        <chargeFullyWhenMade>true</chargeFullyWhenMade>
        <minShieldSize>2.1</minShieldSize>
        <maxShieldSize>2.7</maxShieldSize>
        <disableRotation>true</disableRotation>
      </li>
    </comps>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="VEF.Apparels.ApparelExtension">
        <priority>1</priority>
        <traitsOnEquip>
          <li>VFEP_WarcasketTrait</li>
        </traitsOnEquip>
        <traitsOnUnequip>
          <li>VFEP_Shellcasket</li>
        </traitsOnUnequip>
        <pawnCapacityMinLevels>
          <li>
            <capacity>Moving</capacity>
            <minLevel>0.7</minLevel>
          </li>
          <li>
            <capacity>Manipulation</capacity>
            <minLevel>0.7</minLevel>
          </li>
        </pawnCapacityMinLevels>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </VFEPirates.WarcasketDef>
</Defs>
